# ludic.shooter — the builtin top-down Shooter controller (#60).
#
# A twin-stick / mouse-aim character whose movement is decoupled from aim, a
# data-driven weapon registry, and a general projectile system (pierce / bounce /
# homing / bullet-hell patterns), all conforming to the six-lever contract (#57).
# Reuses the engine Body/Collider and the ludic.gameplay Faction + Combat + Stats
# foundation: the SAME weapon/projectile systems drive a player and an NPC (the AI
# writes the "fire" intent instead of input), so there is no duplicate enemy-gun
# code. Deterministic integer/fixed maths throughout, so bullet patterns replay.
package "ludic.shooter"
version "0.1.0"
kind source
provides "TopDown"
provides "Weapon"
provides "Spawner"
require "ludic.gameplay" "0.1.0"
